    "status": "proposed_not_implemented_for_all_profiles",
    "source": "Printed card pixels and reviewed printed_* fields on cards and card_faces; English Oracle text is not printed-language ground truth.",
    "normalization": "Preserve source text; NFC evaluation by default. Any presentation-form, private-use or compatibility mapping must be explicit and versioned. Do not apply English ASCII folding.",
    "fields": "Keep main title, type, rules, reminder, flavor and footer regions distinct; retain original-pixel bounds and field orientations.",
    "symbols": "Use a versioned shared token mapping for mana, tap and other symbols without translating surrounding text.",
    "direction": "Keep logical transcription and visual reading-order metadata separately; Arabic/Hebrew shaping and Japanese vertical fields need matching training/inference transforms.",
    "fictional_scripts": "Freeze glyph-to-token and font-encoding mappings; expose transliteration or translation as separate fields.",
    "evaluation": "Hold out complete card identities/print families, report each profile and text role separately at clean and multiple blur levels; mark missing labels/evidence explicitly."
